---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Workout Planner & Log with PR Tracker | Nawtch"
  description="Build workout programs, log every set as you train, and track your personal records. Free, no account, and your data stays on your device."
  canonicalPath="/programs/"
  ads="full"
>
  <header>
    <div class="header-left">
      <h1>Workout Planner &amp; Log</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">Build workout programs, log your sets as you train, and track your personal records.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;flex-direction: column;">
      <button style="align-self: auto;" class="add-btn" onclick="window.pgOpenCreate()">+ New Program</button>
      <button style="align-self: auto;" class="ghost-btn pg-exercise-manage-btn" onclick="window.pgOpenExLibrary()">Exercise Library</button>
    </div>
  </header>
  <div class="wt-toggle pg-tabs" id="pg-tabs"></div>
  <div id="pg-active-banner"></div>
  <div id="programs-list"></div>
  <div id="pg-log" style="display:none;"></div>
  <div class="info-banners" id="pg-info-programs">
    <div class="info-banner">
      <div class="info-banner-header" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
        <div class="info-dot" style="background:var(--accent);box-shadow:0 0 6px var(--accent);"></div>
        <span class="info-banner-label" style="color:var(--accent);">Start a workout from any day</span>
        <span class="info-banner-chevron">▼</span>
      </div>
      <div class="info-banner-body">
        Open a program and tap <strong>Start</strong> on a day. Sets, reps, and weight fill in from the program, or
        from your last session if the program leaves them blank. See the <strong>Workout Log</strong> tab for how
        logging works, your past workouts, and personal records.
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="info-banner">
      <div class="info-banner-header" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
        <div class="info-dot" style="background:var(--accent2);box-shadow:0 0 6px var(--accent2);"></div>
        <span class="info-banner-label info-label-warn">Each program can have up to 7 days</span>
        <span class="info-banner-chevron">▼</span>
      </div>
      <div class="info-banner-body">
        A program can hold up to <strong>7 days</strong>, and every day needs at least one exercise before you
        can save. A program always keeps at least one day — once you're down to the last one, its <strong>Remove</strong> option disappears.
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="info-banner">
      <div class="info-banner-header" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
        <div class="info-dot" style="background:var(--muted);box-shadow: 0 0 6px var(--muted);"></div>
        <span class="info-banner-label info-label-info">Your exercise library is shared across all programs</span>
        <span class="info-banner-chevron">▼</span>
      </div>
      <div class="info-banner-body">
        Exercises you create are saved to a shared <strong>Exercise Library</strong> you can search and reuse in
        any program, not just the one you built it in. Adding one to a day copies its current sets, reps, and
        notes at that moment — later edits to the library update future additions, but won't retroactively
        change copies already placed in other programs' days.
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="info-banner">
      <div class="info-banner-header" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
        <div class="info-dot" style="background:var(--carbs);box-shadow: 0 0 6px var(--carbs);"></div>
        <span class="info-banner-label info-label-warn-2">Reorder exercises within a day anytime</span>
        <span class="info-banner-chevron">▼</span>
      </div>
      <div class="info-banner-body">
        Use the <strong>↑</strong>/<strong>↓</strong> arrows next to each exercise to reorder it within a day.
        The library itself — creating, editing, or deleting exercises — can also be managed on its own via the <strong>Exercise Library</strong> button, independent of any specific program.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="info-banners" id="pg-info-log" style="display:none;">
    <div class="info-banner">
      <div class="info-banner-header" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
        <div class="info-dot" style="background:var(--accent);box-shadow:0 0 6px var(--accent);"></div>
        <span class="info-banner-label" style="color:var(--accent);">Your workout saves as you go</span>
        <span class="info-banner-chevron">▼</span>
      </div>
      <div class="info-banner-body">
        Every check and edit is saved on this device right away. You can close the tab, refresh, or lock your
        phone, then pick up where you left off with <strong>Resume workout</strong>. Only one workout can be in
        progress at a time. A workout is dated the day you started it, even if you finish after midnight.
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="info-banner">
      <div class="info-banner-header" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
        <div class="info-dot" style="background:var(--accent2);box-shadow:0 0 6px var(--accent2);"></div>
        <span class="info-banner-label info-label-warn">Logging sets</span>
        <span class="info-banner-chevron">▼</span>
      </div>
      <div class="info-banner-body">
        Tap <strong>✓</strong> to mark a set done. Change the weight or reps first if you did something different
        from the plan. <strong>Mark all as planned</strong> checks every set at once. Leave weight blank for a
        bodyweight set, shown as <strong>BW</strong>. Only checked sets are saved as completed when you tap <strong>Finish</strong>. Exercises you add during a workout stay in that workout only, unless you tick <strong>Also add to this program</strong>.
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="info-banner">
      <div class="info-banner-header" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
        <div class="info-dot" style="background:var(--carbs);box-shadow: 0 0 6px var(--carbs);"></div>
        <span class="info-banner-label info-label-warn-2">How personal records work</span>
        <span class="info-banner-chevron">▼</span>
      </div>
      <div class="info-banner-body">
        <strong>Heaviest</strong> is your heaviest checked set, with its reps. <strong>Most reps</strong> is your
        highest rep count in one set, with its weight. On a tie, the set with more reps or more weight wins. <strong>Est. 1RM</strong> averages the Epley and Brzycki formulas and only uses sets of 1 to 10 reps.
        Timed exercises track your longest time. A small <strong>PR</strong> tag shows on a set that beats a
        record during a workout.
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="info-banner">
      <div class="info-banner-header" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
        <div class="info-dot" style="background:var(--muted);box-shadow: 0 0 6px var(--muted);"></div>
        <span class="info-banner-label info-label-info">Past workouts don't change when programs do</span>
        <span class="info-banner-chevron">▼</span>
      </div>
      <div class="info-banner-body">
        Each workout keeps the program and exercise names and values from the day you did it. Renaming or deleting
        a program or exercise later won't change it. Tap a workout to view, edit, or delete it. Records update to
        match.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="field-hint" style="display:block;margin-top:14px;">
    Track your strength and endurance with our <a href="/calculators/one-rep-max/">One-Rep Max</a> and <a href="/calculators/vo2-max/">VO2 Max</a> calculators. Log your supplements here too → <a href="/supplements/tracker/">Supplement Tracker</a>
  </p>

  <script src="../../islands/vanilla/programs/programs.js"></script>
</BaseLayout>
